# Codebase Structure

## Directory Layout

```
src/
├── main.rs          # Entry point
├── admin.rs         # Admin console commands (SHOW, RELOAD, etc.)
├── client.rs        # Client connection handling
├── server.rs        # Server (PostgreSQL backend) connection handling
├── proto.rs         # PostgreSQL protocol parsing/generation
├── pooler.rs        # Connection pooling logic
├── objects.rs       # Core data structures (PgSocket, PgDatabase, PgPool, etc.)
├── sbuf.rs          # Socket buffer abstraction
├── scram.rs         # SCRAM authentication
├── hba.rs           # Host-based authentication (pg_hba.conf parsing)
├── loader.rs        # Configuration loading
├── janitor.rs       # Maintenance tasks (cleanup, stats)
├── stats.rs         # Statistics collection
├── varcache.rs      # PostgreSQL parameter caching
├── prepare.rs       # Prepared statement handling
├── messages.rs      # Protocol message definitions
├── dnslookup.rs     # DNS resolution
├── pktbuf.rs        # Packet buffer handling
├── takeover.rs      # Online restart / socket takeover
├── util.rs          # Utility functions
├── system.rs        # System-level operations
├── pam.rs           # PAM authentication
├── ldapauth.rs      # LDAP authentication
└── common/          # Shared utilities (crypto, string handling, types)
    ├── types.rs     # Shared type definitions
    ├── cryptohash.rs
    ├── scram_common.rs
    ├── string.rs
    └── ...

lib/usual/           # "libusual" support library (also c2rust translated)
├── tls/             # TLS handling (OpenSSL wrappers)
└── ...              # Various utilities

test/                # Integration tests (Python/pytest)
```

## Key Data Structures (in objects.rs)

- `PgSocket` — Represents a client or server connection
- `PgDatabase` — Database configuration
- `PgPool` — Connection pool for a database/user pair
- `PgUser` — User credentials and settings
- `PgStats` — Statistics counters

## Module Dependencies (high-level)

```
main
 └── pooler (event loop)
      ├── client (client connections)
      │    ├── proto (protocol)
      │    ├── scram/hba (auth)
      │    └── sbuf (I/O)
      ├── server (backend connections)
      │    ├── proto
      │    └── sbuf
      ├── admin (admin commands)
      └── janitor (maintenance)

objects ← used by almost everything
loader  ← configuration, used at startup
```

## lib/usual

This is a translated version of "libusual", a C utility library. Contains:
- TLS/OpenSSL wrappers
- Event loop primitives
- Socket utilities
- Logging

Treat as lower-level infrastructure. Refactor `src/` modules first.

## Global State Locations

Major globals (to eventually wrap in thread-local):
- `database_list`, `pool_list`, `user_list` — in objects.rs
- `cf_*` config variables — scattered, many in loader.rs
- Statistics counters — in stats.rs

## Protocol Flow

1. Client connects → `client.rs` handles handshake
2. Authentication → `scram.rs`, `hba.rs`, `pam.rs`, or `ldapauth.rs`
3. Query → routed through pooler to available server connection
4. Server response → forwarded back to client
5. Connection returned to pool or closed
